<p>The one style that breaks the rule about the accent — the whole ground is the accent — and that is exactly why it reads as a skit from across the room. White dots on the red, the person big and centred, the title in the hand at four and a half em with a hard shadow, and two stickers (chips ringed with the canvas, tilted) that say what it is. The mark goes on a canvas tile so it reads on the red.</p>
